  "result": "Quiz 0002 is ready. It has six questions on O4, the difference between workflows and agents and when a fixed workflow is the better choice. Its files are `quizzes/0002.json` and `keys/0002.json`.\n\n- **The questions:** There are four multiple-choice items, one short answer and one numeric item. Each one ties to the makerspace assistant. They cover who owns the control flow, classifying real designs, a hybrid design, which part of the assistant suits a fixed workflow, and the token cost difference.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** No lesson covers O4 yet, so this quiz checks the objective directly. I wrote it from the standard definition: in a workflow, predefined code sets the path, and in an agent, the model directs its own steps and tool use. I didn't search the web for a source, so the quiz isn't cited.\n- **Misconception ids:** The key has no `distractors` field. I couldn't see what the existing ids M1, M3, M4 and M6 stand for, and I didn't want to tag them wrongly. The wrong-answer patterns are in each item's rationale instead.\n\nDo you want a short lesson on O4 before you take it? Otherwise, send me your answers when you're ready and I'll grade them.",
